>> title: Soy Sauce Pan-Fried Noodles
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: noodles, soy sauce, bean sprouts, hong kong, stovetop, quick
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: si yau wong chau min, 豉油皇炒麵, soy sauce pan fried noodles, soy sauce chow mein, king soy sauce noodles, soy sauce fried noodles
>> servings: 2
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: narrow — a crowded pan steams instead of browning, and noodles that have gone wet and soft will not come back however long you leave them over the heat

A home burner will not scorch these. Dry the noodles hard and fry them in two batches for what browning you can get.

>> step: stir it together, no cornstarch
Stir @dark soy sauce{1%Tbs}, @light soy sauce{2%tsp}, @sugar{1%tsp} and @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp} together in a bowl.

>> step: loosen 1 min, drain and dry hard
Loosen @fresh thin egg noodles{12%oz}(340 g; the ones sold for chow mein) in a #saucepan{} of boiling water for ~boil{1%min}, then drain them and spread them out to dry.

>> step: fry flat 5 min, two batches, still between turns
Fry @&(~1)noodles{} in @neutral oil{2%Tbs} in a #frying pan{} for ~fry{5%min} in two batches, pressing them flat and leaving them alone between turns.

>> step: toss 1 min and get it out of the pan
Toss @&(~1)noodles{} with @&(~3)sauce{}, @bean sprouts{2%cups}(150 g), @scallions{3}(cut in 2-in lengths) and @white pepper{1/4%tsp} for ~fry{1%min}, and get it out of the pan while the sprouts still snap.
